838: 			/* NOTE: this will NOT stall the file. The reason is that when a new file
839: 			 * with the same name is detected, we will not run into this code.
840: 			 TODO: check the full implications, there are for sure some!
841: 			       e.g. file has been closed, so we will never have old inode (but
842: 			            why was it closed then? --> check)
843: 			 */
